@page "/privacy-policy"
@layout KonXProWebApp.Components.Layout.LandingLayout

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy — KonXPro</PageTitle>

<div class="legal-page-container" style="max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 24px 96px 24px; color: var(--text-secondary, #94a3b8); line-height: 1.7;">
    <div style="margin-bottom: 36px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default, #1e293b); padding-bottom: 24px;">
        <span style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--color-primary-light, #60a5fa);">Legal & Compliance</span>
        <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-top: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted, #64748b); margin: 0;">Effective Date: September 1, 2026 · Last Updated: September 2026</p>
    </div>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-bottom: 12px;">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>KonXPro ("we," "our," or "us") provides building permit intelligence, lead pipeline management, and market analytics to licensed trade contractors and construction professionals across the five boroughs of New York City. This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your personal information when you visit our website at <strong style="color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc);">konxpro.com</strong>, create an account, or subscribe to our services.</p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-bottom: 12px;">2. NYC Department of Buildings (DOB) Public Records Notice</h2>
        <p>KonXPro ingests, indexes, and surfaces building permit filings, job applications, violations, and associated public records published by the New York City Department of Buildings ("NYC DOB") and the City of New York via official Open Data portals.</p>
        <div style="background: rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary, #2563eb); padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 4px; margin: 16px 0;">
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc);"><strong>Public Record Disclaimer:</strong> Property addresses, permit categories, estimated job costs, filing dates, applicant identities, and owner contact details displayed in our permit feeds and lead dossiers are sourced directly from public government records. KonXPro does not alter official public records and is not an agency or affiliate of the City of New York or the NYC Department of Buildings.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-bottom: 12px;">3. Information We Collect from Subscribers</h2>
        <p>When you register, configure alert preferences, or purchase a subscription, we collect:</p>
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
            <li><strong>Account & Profile Information:</strong> Name, business name, trade license numbers, business email, phone number, and account credentials.</li>
            <li><strong>Territory & Alert Preferences:</strong> Designated trade specialties, target boroughs, neighborhoods, job valuation thresholds, and notification delivery options (Email, SMS, push).</li>
            <li><strong>Billing & Payment Data:</strong> Credit card and billing details are transmitted directly to our PCI-DSS Level 1 certified payment processor (Stripe). KonXPro does not store complete credit card numbers on its servers.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage & Technical Data:</strong> IP addresses, browser types, device identifiers, referral URLs, and interactions with our application components.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-bottom: 12px;">4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We utilize subscriber information exclusively for legitimate business and operational purposes:</p>
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
            <li>Dispatching real-time permit notifications and daily email digests according to your configured trade filters.</li>
            <li>Provisioning subscriber accounts, processing recurring subscription payments, and enforcing tier limits.</li>
            <li>Monitoring platform stability, diagnosing server performance, and securing against unauthorized access.</li>
            <li>Communicating product updates, system maintenance windows, and customer support responses.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>We do not sell, rent, or trade your subscriber personal information to third parties.</strong></p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-bottom: 12px;">5. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
        <p>We share necessary data with trusted infrastructure and service providers operating under strict confidentiality obligations:</p>
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
            <li><strong>Stripe:</strong> Payment processing, customer portal management, and recurring billing.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Hosting:</strong> Microsoft Azure for resilient, encrypted cloud application hosting and SQL database services in the United States.</li>
            <li><strong>Notification Gateways:</strong> Enterprise SMS and transactional email dispatch providers for alert delivery.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-bottom: 12px;">6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We retain active subscriber account information for the duration of your active subscription and up to twenty-four (24) months thereafter to comply with tax, legal, and financial auditing standards. Public permit filings are retained and indexed historically to power longitudinal analytics and market reporting.</p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-bottom: 12px;">7. Your Rights & Choices</h2>
        <p>Subject to applicable state and federal privacy statutes (including CCPA/CPRA and applicable New York state privacy regulations), you have the right to:</p>
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
            <li>Access, correct, or review personal information associated with your subscriber account.</li>
            <li>Request deletion of your account and associated personal identifiers upon cancellation.</li>
            <li>Opt out of marketing communications or adjust notification frequencies at any time via Account Settings.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc); margin-bottom: 12px;">8. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>For questions or requests concerning this Privacy Policy or data processing practices, please contact:</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 8px;">
            <strong style="color: var(--text-primary, #f8fafc);">KonXPro Compliance & Privacy Office</strong><br>
            Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@konxpro.com" style="color: var(--color-primary-light, #60a5fa); text-decoration: underline;">privacy@konxpro.com</a><br>
            Support: <a href="mailto:support@konxpro.com" style="color: var(--color-primary-light, #60a5fa); text-decoration: underline;">support@konxpro.com</a><br>
            New York, NY
        </p>
    </section>
</div>

